why Every Horde quest of Ragefire Chasm in one run, lead-ins included.

# Ragefire Chasm's Horde quests in one guide: Thrall's Hidden Enemies in
# Orgrimmar, the pick-ups in Thunder Bluff and the Undercity, one run through
# the chasm, then the hand-ins. Steps already done are passed over, so the
# guide picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The chain: Thrall's 5726 Hidden Enemies (a Lieutenant's Insignia from the
# Burning Blade in Durotar) -> 5727 (a word with Neeru Fireblade) -> 5728
# (Bazzalan and Jergosh the Invoker) -> 5729 (to Neeru) -> 5730 (back to
# Thrall). Neeru Fireblade's 5761 Slaying the Beast (Taragaman the Hungerer's
# heart). Rahauro's 5723 Testing an Enemy's Strength (troggs and shamans) and
# 5722 Searching for the Lost Satchel (Maur Grimtotem's corpse inside) ->
# 5724 Returning the Lost Satchel. Varimathras' 5725 The Power to Destroy...
# (two books from the Searing Blade).
#
# Left out: none of the Horde's. Ragefire Chasm is a city dungeon of the
# Horde (its door is in Orgrimmar), so the pack has no Alliance guide for it.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses or Maur Grimtotem inside, so
# their goals stand at the door (@49.3,95.1, Orgrimmar) with `group 5`. The
# bosses come in the order of the client's dungeon journal (Oggleflint,
# Taragaman the Hungerer, Jergosh the Invoker, Bazzalan), not of a recorded
# run. Every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a group that takes
# them in another order still gets each step ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items and rewards: Polestar's reference data (data/forever,
#   built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's Codex page for
#   the dungeon. The insignia drops from the Burning Blade Fanatics and
#   Apprentices (level 9 to 11), the books from the Searing Blade Cultists and
#   Warlocks inside.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   13 to 18).
# INGAME: where inside does Maur Grimtotem's corpse lie?

